# Docker Desktop restarts with the rs27-mini project from 02 running (SANDBOX_COMPUTER_EGRESS=restricted).
# Restart command: Windows' own CLI, "C:\Program Files\Docker\Docker\resources\bin\docker.exe" desktop restart.
# (The WSL distro's `docker desktop restart` fails here: it tries to start /opt/docker-desktop/bin/com.docker.backend,
#  a Docker Desktop for Linux path, and leaves Docker Desktop running.)
# Restart policies: computer-egress, supervisor, relay-standin, web unless-stopped; bot computers RestartPolicy=no.
# after-restart.sh records container start times, the rule count (vm-rules.sh count), the supervisor's egress log
# lines, then resumes the computer through the supervisor (no supervisor restart) and probes it.

## 0. Two engine restarts not started by this test (08:34:17 and 08:34:54, while a question to the Self-hoster was open)
sidecar "apk add" finished at 08:34:28 and 08:34:54; supervisor "supervisor listening" 08:34:31 and 08:34:56
supervisor 08:35:03 "restricted computer egress verified"
rakazo-bot-rs27bot exited 08:34:17 (exit 0; RestartPolicy=no)
the supervisor's startup egress-probe container (created 08:34:31, computer image, no AutoRemove) was killed by the
08:34:54 restart (exit 137) and left behind; found and removed during cleanup

